#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
nr-xjukebox (2026-09-12) -- the X lane's bot for Noderunners Radio, speaking as @JukeboxLNDbot.
A listener posts "@JukeboxLNDbot play <song> | <message>". The bot asks the station for a one-time pay code and
answers ONCE with the link to the station's own pay page. The page does the rest (every match listed, invoice, queued).
When the song goes ON AIR this bot quote-posts the listener's own request (SF 2026-09-13); the announcer skips
X-lane songs. Charter: plan/x-jukebox/CHARTER-v4.html (every rule binds).

HOW IT WORKS
  1  Every 30 s it reads the bot's mentions on X (max 5 posts, since the last one; on the very first start "since now",
     so no backlog is ever read or billed). Every read is written in the book BEFORE the call, at 5 x the read price,
     and corrected to what really came back. Empty polls cost nothing.
  2  Every post passes the charter's checks in order: opt-out ("stop") first; is it for the bot (starts with "play" after
     the leading @names; no retweets, quotes or long posts; at most ONE friend tagged); younger than 3 minutes (by X's
     own clock); never answered before (edits are skipped); this person under 3 a day, no code still open, 20 s since the
     last one; 20 replies an hour lane-wide; the purse and the daily limit; the announcer's word list over the query and
     the message (a hit = silence).
  3  The station mints a code for the search at the price of the day. The bot writes "being answered" to disk, books the
     reply in the ledger, THEN posts the reply, THEN marks it sent. A crash in between never gives anyone two replies.
  4  A live sesh (the station says 409) gets one answer per person per sesh. A search the station refuses as empty gets
     the friendly "nothing aboard" answer with the jukebox link. Anything else: silence. Never a second reply.
  5  Every open code is watched (station, every 60 s). When its song shows up on /api/nowplaying as a paid X request,
     the sats go in the book: the on-air post is booked as the lane's cost, the sats become dollars by the rate rule
     (two sources, fresh, agreeing, the lower one, minus 10 %), or wait in the book as sats until a rate passes.
  6  The purse is the sum of the book. It is recounted from the file at every start and after every line. Below the
     price of the next action: the lane goes quiet and SF hears it once on Telegram.

THE PURSE (files in /home/sf/.config/nr-xjukebox/; NR_XJUKEBOX_HOME overrides the folder)
  ledger.tsv           append-only: ts_utc  kind  usd  sats  ref. Kinds: seed topup read read_adjust reply onair income
                       unconverted rate. Spend is negative, income positive. The float = the sum of the usd column.
  seed-usd             SF's hand: the dollars loaded at X. Missing = 0 = quiet. Every change is booked once (seed/topup).
  budget-usd-per-day   the daily limit (the installer writes 0.50). Reached: no polling, no replies until 00:00 UTC.
  console-cap-usd      the monthly cap set at X (default 60): the lane pauses at 70 % of it, the announcer's posts counted.
  prices.json          X's prices as booked; floors are hard-coded (read 0.005, reply 0.010, post 0.015, user 0.010):
                       the file may raise them, never lower them. read_owned (0.001) and margin (1.5) feed the song price.
  price-sats           the song's price today, set once a day from the formula in the charter (100..500). SF may
                       overwrite it by hand: a hand-edited file wins and the bot stops writing it; delete it to resume.
  codes.json           open / minted / paid codes with their sats and times.       state.json   everything else.
  optout.txt           people who said "stop" (never answered again).   ignore.txt   people with 3 trips in a day, a week.
  balance-check        exists -> once a day, around the first live reply, GET /2/usage/credits is tried and logged.

SWITCHES (no restart needed)
  OFF     exists -> nothing runs, zero spend.
  LIVE    absent -> PRACTICE MODE: reads (they cost cents), runs every check, logs "[practice] would reply" and posts
          NOTHING, mints NOTHING.   Present -> the real thing.

TELEGRAM (through the station's admin-notes channel; the same event at most once per 6 h)
  purse empty, daily limit hit, credits out (402), keys refused (401), a run of refusals, a code minted but no reply
  sent, a rate rejected, the station down for 6 h, and one line a day at 20:00 UTC with the day's numbers.
  TODO (not in v1): a short ping to the group tagging @noderunnersfm/@plebroyale when money stops (needs the Telegram
  bot; config key group_ping in state is a placeholder).

RUN  (systemd: nr-xjukebox.service, User=sf)     nr-xjukebox
     nr-xjukebox --check      state and settings, no network, spends nothing
     nr-xjukebox --once       one cycle under the same lock as the service
     nr-xjukebox --selftest   the built-in cases; nothing leaves the box
